  clock: 1  # 805f
  nonce: 805f  # 805f
  data:  # 805f
    kind: work_item  # 805f
    title: "rust: a Rust 2024 'unsafe extern' block does not parse in the shipped tree-sitter-rust, so its declarations get no symbol and calls to them stay external stubs (11146 such block lines in the corpus)"  # 805f
    status: todo_hard  # 805f
    priority: 3  # 805f
    parent:  # 805f
    tags:  # 805f
    - rust  # 805f
    - analysis_quality  # 805f
    - io_boundary  # 805f
    isbefore: []  # 805f
    duplicate_of: []  # 805f
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 805f
    pr_ref:  # 805f
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-04 while fixing INV-lopus-mamoz-tokum-padab-mivuv-vomum-gosal-votit (branch jgstern-agent/fix/lopus, not integrated).\n\nThe shipped tree-sitter-rust (0.24.0) does not parse a Rust 2024 `unsafe extern \"C\" { ... }` block. It yields a top-level function_signature_item carrying function_modifiers + an ERROR node, and a stray ERROR for the closing brace. No foreign_mod_item exists, so the INV-lopus extern-block arm (which requires item -> declaration_list -> foreign_mod_item) emits no symbol for any declaration in it, and a call to one stays an `external` stub exactly as before INV-lopus.\n\nPinned as a stated gap by test_rust_extern_block_symbols.py::test_a_signature_outside_any_block_is_no_foreign_symbol.\n\nPOPULATION (grep, corpus ~/whole_bunch_of_repos, lines matching `^\\s*unsafe extern( \"..\")? *\\{`): 11146, of which pdfium-render 11056 (bindgen output under src/bindgen/, which the survey does not analyse at all), wasmtime 82, nextjs 3. Plain `extern {}` blocks: 146. bindgen >= 0.71 emits the unsafe form, so the share grows with every regenerated binding.\n\nNOT MEASURED: whether a newer tree-sitter-rust grammar parses the form (no network check made); how many calls into these declarations hit a catalogue row by short name.\n\nDIRECTION: upgrade the grammar if a release parses it; otherwise recognise the error-recovery shape (function_signature_item whose function_modifiers holds an extern_modifier, at a level no block encloses) as a foreign declaration."  # 805f
    fields: {}  # 805f
- op: discuss  # 2256
  at: '2026-10-05T04:43:30Z'  # 2256
  by: agent  # 2256
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2256
  clock: 2  # 2256
  nonce: '2256'  # 2256
  message: "Integrator 2026-10-05: tree-sitter-rust 0.24.2 (the floor since PR #1459, commit 1856bcf2fe) parses Rust 2024 'unsafe extern \"C\" { pub safe fn getpid() -> i32; }' as a foreign_mod_item (only the safe qualifier is an ERROR leaf), and the analyzer emits getpid as a foreign function with ffi_import {abi: C}; pinned by test_rust_extern_block_symbols.py::test_a_rust_2024_unsafe_extern_block_declares_its_functions. Not checked: the 11,146 corpus block lines this item counted; re-measure before closing."  # 2256
